Chapter: Fat16ZeroRoot

  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 A zeroed disk mounts as the zero volume, the answer every refused BPB gets:
 bytes per sector 0, no root entries, no clusters. A root lookup, listing and
 create on it must answer nothing, not divide by the zero sector size.

Section: Reporting

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing = act
    vol <- fat16-init 2048
    print-line-uni ("bps " & show (vol.vol-bytes-per-sector))
    f <- fat16-find-in-root vol "A.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("find " & (when f is Just (e) -> "found" is None -> "none"))
    r <- fat16-root-entries vol
    print-line-uni ("root entries " & show (list-length r))
    c <- fat16-create-file vol "A.TXT" fat16-src-empty
    print-line-uni ("create " & yn c)
    print-line-uni ("root sectors " & show (fat16-root-sector-count vol))
  end
